### 7. AI Visuals

AI Visuals use Artificial Intelligence capabilities within Power BI to provide advanced insights automatically. These 
visuals help users identify patterns and trends without writing complex code. AI visuals simplify data analysis and 
improve decision-making. They can automatically identify hidden relationships and unusual patterns within data.
Businesses use AI visuals for predictive analysis and discovering insights that may be difficult to identify
manually.

**Types of AI Visuals:**

* Key Influencers
* Decomposition Tree
* Q&A Visual
* Smart Narrative
* Anomaly Detection

**Example:**
Key Influencers identifies factors affecting sales performance.

---

### 8. Paginated Reports

Paginated Reports are designed for printing and creating highly formatted documents. They display complete datasets 
across multiple pages with exact formatting. These reports are ideal for invoices and financial reports. Paginated
reports provide highly structured document layouts and support detailed information presentation. Businesses use 
them when exact formatting and professional document appearance are necessary.

**Features:**

* Pixel-perfect formatting
* Multi-page reports
* Export to PDF and Excel
* Supports tables and charts

**Example:**
Generating customer invoices for monthly billing.

---

### 9. Power BI Embedded

Power BI Embedded allows developers to integrate Power BI reports and dashboards into custom applications and
websites. Users can view analytics directly inside applications without opening Power BI separately. This improves 
user experience and provides seamless access to business insights. Embedded analytics helps organizations create 
customized applications with interactive reporting features. It also supports secure access and scalable
deployment for enterprise applications.

**Advantages:**

* Custom application integration
* Interactive analytics
* Secure report access
* Scalable deployment

**Example:**
An e-commerce website displays sales analytics within its admin dashboard.
